{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the cheapest Ultahost VPS plan?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Ultahost's entry managed VPS plan is VPS Basic at $9.19/month on a 24-month term (renews at $5.52/month for 2 years). It includes 1 vCPU AMD EPYC, 1 GB DDR5 RAM, 30 GB NVMe SSD, a dedicated IPv4 address, 4 IPv6 addresses, free SSL, and a 30-day money-back guarantee. The VPS-hosting page advertises VPS starting from about $5/month on longer terms."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Where are Ultahost's data centers located?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Ultahost operates 33+ global data center locations, verified from ultahost.com: Seattle, Dallas, Los Angeles, New York, and Chicago in the United States, plus London, Frankfurt, Amsterdam, Paris, Madrid, Warsaw, Istanbul, Toronto, Singapore, Tokyo, and Sydney, among others. This gives Ultahost one of the broader location footprints among managed VPS providers."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Ultahost VPS managed or unmanaged?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Ultahost offers flexible management tiers: unmanaged (full server control, no pre-installed panel), semi-managed (SSH / WordPress / PHP help from support), and fully managed (updates, patching, and configuration handled for you). Every plan includes full root access for custom software, AI models, and automation workflows."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What virtualization and CPU hardware does Ultahost use?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Ultahost runs KVM virtualization on enterprise-grade SuperMicro hardware with AMD EPYC 4.0-4.2 GHz processors and NVMe SSDs with PCIe Gen 5 architecture. Instances get guaranteed, isolated CPU, RAM, and storage compared to shared hosting."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How does Ultahost compare to RackNerd or Vultr?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Ultahost ($9.19/mo managed entry) is a managed provider with 33+ datacenters and bundled support, so it costs more than RackNerd's bare-budget $1.99/mo unmanaged entry. Vultr's $5/mo unmanaged hourly cloud covers 32+ locations but is fully self-managed. Pick Ultahost if you want managed KVM with a wide location footprint; RackNerd remains the pure-budget leader."}}]}
  </script>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <a href="/vps" class="text-gray-500 hover:text-orange-500 text-sm mb-6 block">← Back to VPS Reviews</a>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-start justify-between mb-8">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Ultahost Review</h1>
        <div class="flex gap-4 text-sm text-gray-400">
          <span>Founded: <strong class="text-orange-500">est. 2017</strong></span>
          <span>Datacenters: <strong>33+ global</strong></span>
          <span>Specialty: <strong>Managed KVM + AMD EPYC</strong></span>
