    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-green-400">Pros</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ 33+ global data centers — among the widest footprints of any managed VPS provider we review</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ AMD EPYC 4.0–4.2 GHz CPUs + NVMe SSD with PCIe Gen 5 architecture</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ Flexible managed / semi-managed / unmanaged tiers — you pick the level of support</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ Unlimited bandwidth on Business and above</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ KVM virtualization with guaranteed, isolated CPU / RAM / storage</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">✅ 30-day money-back guarantee and free SSL on every plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-red-400">Cons</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ $9.19/mo managed entry is 4–5× the bare-budget $1.99/mo unmanaged leaders (RackNerd etc.)</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ Renewal structure: intro price is billed up front on a 24-month term, not true month-to-month</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ Entry-tier (Basic) caps at 1 Gbps; only Business+ gets unlimited bandwidth</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ Port 25 (email sending) is restricted on entry-level plans unless you unlock it at $117+ billing</li>
          <li class="text-gray-300 text-sm">⚠️ No dedicated GPU compute tier — CPU-only KVM</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">Ultahost is a strong pick when you want <strong>managed Linux VPS with a wide global footprint</strong> and don't want to do all the sysadmin yourself. The AMD EPYC + NVMe hardware stack, flexible support tiers, and 33+ locations distinguish it from bare-budget hosts. It is not the cheapest option — the $9.19/mo managed entry is several times RackNerd's $1.99/mo unmanaged tier — so value depends on whether you need the bundled management and coverage. All specs and prices verified live from <a href="https://ultahost.com/vps-hosting" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">ultahost.com/vps-hosting</a> (HTTP 200, August 2026).</p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">For pure-budget unmanaged Linux, see our <a href="/vps/racknerd" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd review</a>. For hourly-billed self-managed cloud at $5/mo, see <a href="/vps/vultr" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Vultr</a>. For another managed-cPanel option, see <a href="/vps/tmdhosting" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">TMDHosting</a>.</p>
    </div>

